the study by Liverpool University and  Imperial College London looked at  sixteen thousand seven hundred and forty  nine people admitted to hospital in the  UK some of these patients are still  being treated for covert nineteen but of  those with outcomes sixty percent were  discharged and sadly forty percent died  Bing male older and having some existing  medical conditions increases a patient's  risk of dying and just over half of the  Cova 19 patients studied here had a  pre-existing condition those with  dementia had the greatest increased risk  of death  39% above average but obesity is also a  key indicator with the chances of dying  increasing by 37 percent although the  range around that number is still quite  wide and clinicians say this link  between obesity and the risk of death  from kovat 19 is no coincidence excess  body fat seems to drive not just  underlying health conditions that coded  19 seems to exploit but excess body fat  also increases chronic inflammation in  the body so mild chronic damage to the  body over a number of years and what  happens with poket 19 is that people  that tragically die from it died because  of an exaggerated immune response that  attacks the lung something called a RDS  or acute respiratory distress syndrome  which ultimately causes death in a  tragic minority of people so let's look  at how the levels of obesity in the UK  compared to other countries around the  world many of which have been hit hard  by kovat 19 the number of covered 19  deaths in the UK is among the highest in  Europe and more than a quarter of adults  some 28% are classed as obese in the  u.s. that figure is more than a third at  36% but in countries with a lower number  of deaths like South Korea in Japan less  than five percent of adults are obese  one thing that is concerning scientists  and researchers is the number of people  from certain ethnic groups dying would  cove at 19 we don't know why  for certain but it could be linked to a  number of factors including obesity a  recent active life survey published by  the Office for National Statistics found  72 percent of the black African and  Caribbean community in the UK are  overweight or obese the highest  proportion of any ethnic group we are  learning more about this Nivelle virus  every day how and who it attacks and the  more information we have about those  most at risk more lives we'll be able to  save
 

